       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day by prescription, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single dose of 1600 mg is also above the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) for severe inflammatory pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day) for general analgesia.\n\nMaybe 1600 mg was meant as the daily total, for example 400 mg four times daily. If so, tell me and I'll enter that. Or tell me which of the options above you want, and any note to add, such as \"take with food\" or a PRN indication."
